1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,450
I thought funding was easy.

2
00:00:02,587 --> 00:00:04,633
Then I got a reality check.

3
00:00:05,353 --> 00:00:07,693
Raising money is difficult.

4
00:00:07,733 --> 00:00:12,083
Investors bet on two things.

5
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:13,720
First: the founder.

6
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:15,267
Second: the company.

7
00:00:15,387 --> 00:00:18,727
A strong founder.

8
00:00:19,087 --> 00:00:21,397
A strong college background.

9
00:00:21,627 --> 00:00:25,367
Or a startup already in the market.

10
00:00:26,047 --> 00:00:27,383
Strong traction.

11
00:00:28,673 --> 00:00:29,853
Good revenue.

12
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:31,567
Real customers.

13
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:36,200
But what if you're just starting?

14
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,830
What do you do then?

15
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:39,920
No elite college background.

16
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:41,770
Just getting started.

17
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:43,630
No funding yet.

18
00:00:43,813 --> 00:00:46,293
What's the next move?

19
00:00:46,473 --> 00:00:48,033
Apply to accelerators.

20
00:00:48,187 --> 00:00:49,977
There are good accelerators.

21
00:00:50,527 --> 00:00:53,017
You may already know

22
00:00:53,017 --> 00:00:56,957
Y Combinator.

23
00:00:56,987 --> 00:00:59,327
Apply to accelerators

24
00:00:59,347 --> 00:01:01,967
if you're at the initial stage.

25
00:01:02,107 --> 00:01:04,533
Comment your point of view.
